WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.620
If you can't beat the heat this May, get inside
and chill with some brand new Netflix programming.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.880
The streaming giant is kicking off the month
with more original films and shows than ever

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.330
before, from screamworthy sci-fi thrillers
to gut-busting comedies.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:18.150
There's going to be something new for everyone
this month, so follow along as we look at

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.640
everything coming to Netflix in May 2018,
starting with the Netflix originals.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.650
Sometimes

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:29.030
This international drama sees seven patients
anxiously waiting in a medical clinic for

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.270
the results of their HIV tests.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:35.410
Impatient, they bribe the attendant to get
the results earlier, then struggle to come

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.470
to terms with the news that one of them is
positive.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.060
Sometimes arrives on May 1st.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:42.990
The Rain: Season 1

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:46.510
Sci-fi thrillers seem to be a popular catch
for Netflix, because the streaming service

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.270
is loading up on new releases in the genre.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:53.731
Netflix first announced their upcoming Danish
series The Rain back in June 2017, and the

00:00:53.731 --> 00:00:59.210
recent teasers showcase a desolate post-apocalyptic
world where being infected with a deadly virus

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.760
is as easy as getting caught in a summer shower.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.519
All eight episodes of The Rain make landfall
on May 4th.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:06.519
Anon

00:01:06.519 --> 00:01:11.749
Starring Clive Owen and Amanda Seyfried, Netflix's
upcoming sci-fi film Anon takes place in a

00:01:11.749 --> 00:01:16.779
future where technology has rendered anonymity,
and as a result, crime, almost nonexistent.

00:01:16.779 --> 00:01:20.789
But when the police land on the trail of a
woman who can apparently hack into people's

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:25.530
neural implants and alter their perceptions
of the world, life suddenly gets a lot more

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.530
dangerous.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:31.170
"Placing a moving image… in real time."

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.060
How do you stop a criminal who can change
what's right in front of your eyes?

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.420
Find out when Anon arrives on May 4th.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:39.420
End Game

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.160
This new documentary from filmmakers Jeffrey
Friedman and Rob Epstein explores life at

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.450
the end of the line.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.259
What do people feel as their final days approach?

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:51.799
Through a series of interviews with hospice
patients and people on life support, End Game

00:01:51.799 --> 00:01:54.889
looks for answers to life's toughest questions.

00:01:54.889 --> 00:01:56.899
Look for it on May 4th.

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:58.899
Dear White People: Season 2

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:03.771
This satirical comedy generated a lot of controversy
when it was released in 2017, but went on

00:02:03.771 --> 00:02:08.289
to earn critical praise for its portrayal
of race and discrimination in a mostly white

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:09.920
upper class college.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.140
Each episode of the series hones in on a different
character, exploring their relationships with

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.310
their fellow classmates.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:19.820
Fans have been eagerly awaiting the second
season for months, and the wait is finally

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.320
over on May 4th.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.320
Manhunt

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:28.170
Netflix's upcoming thriller Manhunt centers
on a Chinese lawyer who's been framed for

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.170
murder.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.860
To clear his name, he has to team up with
a Japanese detective to uncover the real reasons

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:33.860
behind the frame-up.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.460
Directed by kung-fu action icon John Woo,
Manhunt looks like an edge-of-your-seat thrill

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.340
ride that's definitely worth keeping on your
radar for May 4th.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:43.820
Forgive Us Our Debts

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:48.790
In this Italian film, a man deeply in debt
is forced to start working for a violent enforcer

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.760
to collect other people's debts.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.250
As he gets more involved in his new job, he
begins to suspect that his new boss and mentor

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:58.490
is worse than he could have ever imagined.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.650
Forgive Us Our Debts premieres on May 4th.

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.690
Busted!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.550
This show looks ridiculous.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:09.070
It's a Korean detective comedy-slash-variety
show, and each episode will see the motley

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.370
clue crew solving a different mystery.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.870
Are all their cases connected?

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:13.870
We have no idea!

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:17.840
The description says that there's one big
mystery behind the show, but based on the

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.430
trailer, we don't even know exactly what that
means.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:24.320
Take a look, if you dare, on May 4th.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.260
A Little Help with Carol Burnett

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.790
Comedian Carol Burnett made a name for herself
in the '70s with her sketch comedy series

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.060
The Carol Burnett Show, and she's been trucking
along ever since.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.710
Now, she'll join the Netflix ranks with A
Little Help with Carol Burnett, a series that

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:42.660
will see the comedy icon and her celebrity
guests learn the ins and outs of the modern

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.010
world with a little help from tech-savvy children.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.240
"Stay woke."

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.780
"Stay woke?

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:51.640
…I will."

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.420
Check it out on May 4th.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.490
Safe: Season 1

00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:01.120
Michael C. Hall hasn't graced the small screen
much since Dexter wrapped in 2013, but this

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.990
month will mark his triumphant return as he
headlines the upcoming series Safe.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:10.770
In Safe, Hall stars as a father of two who
has to take matters into his own hands when

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.540
one of his daughters goes missing.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.380
As he digs deeper into his seemingly perfect
suburban community, he finds more skeletons

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.229
than he ever expected.

00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:22.599
The entire first season of Safe drops on May
10th.

00:04:22.599 --> 00:04:25.210
Bill Nye Saves the World: Season 3

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:30.250
The Science Guy is back again with a new season
of his Netflix show Bill Nye Saves the World.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:34.080
The series hasn't been met with a lot of fan
praise so far, although audiences did seem

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.139
to warm up to Nye a little during the second
season.

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:41.800
In the upcoming third season, Bill Nye will
tackle issues including evolution, food science,

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:44.449
and stem cells with a host of celebrity guest
stars.

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:46.789
Check it out on May 11th.

00:04:46.789 --> 00:04:48.439
The Kissing Booth

00:04:48.439 --> 00:04:52.349
Based on the book of the same name, The Kissing
Booth is a teen drama about a girl who finds

00:04:52.349 --> 00:04:56.870
herself face to face with the hottest boy
in school, and her longtime crush, in a carnival

00:04:56.870 --> 00:04:58.259
kissing booth.

00:04:58.259 --> 00:05:02.009
Should she kiss him, even though he's also
the brother of her best friend?

00:05:02.009 --> 00:05:06.930
Keep a defibrillator on hand, because these
plot twists are truly heartstopping.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.960
Look for The Kissing Booth on May 11th.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.659
Evil Genius

00:05:11.659 --> 00:05:15.629
Netflix brings something new to the documentary
table every month, and this May they're adding

00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:21.020
Evil Genius, a four-part series on the so-called
"pizza bomber heist" that happened in Pennsylvania

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.300
in 2003.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.449
The robbery involved a pizza delivery man
who walked into a bank with a bomb collar

00:05:26.449 --> 00:05:27.750
around his neck.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.080
Evil Genius examines new details in the case
and takes a closer look at the mastermind

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.499
behind the whole, messed up episode.

00:05:34.499 --> 00:05:38.050
Tune in for all the twists and turns on May
11th.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.050
Cargo

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.379
Starring Martin Freeman, Cargo is about a
man in a zombie apocalypse who has to find

00:05:43.379 --> 00:05:48.080
a way to care for his infant child even though
he himself is becoming infected.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.680
Cargo is based on the 2013 short film of the
same name, which is one of the most emotional

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.900
six and a half minutes you're likely to watch
anytime soon.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:59.990
If the film is as good as the short, and can
manage to offer some fresh surprises, it's

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.319
bound to be a hit.

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:04.669
Look for Cargo to stream on Netflix on May
18th.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:05.699
Catching Feelings

00:06:05.699 --> 00:06:11.189
After premiering at the Los Angeles Film Festival
in 2017, this critically praised South African

00:06:11.189 --> 00:06:15.229
comedy finally snagged a distributor in the
form of Netflix.

00:06:15.229 --> 00:06:19.789
The story is a quiet look at a young teacher
and his wife whose lives suddenly change when

00:06:19.789 --> 00:06:21.620
a famous writer moves in with them.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.849
Equal parts hilarious and heartwarming, Catching
Feelings looks like another great addition

00:06:25.849 --> 00:06:27.280
to the Netflix lineup.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.259
Check it out on May 18th.

00:06:29.259 --> 00:06:31.969
Mob Psycho 100: Season 1

00:06:31.969 --> 00:06:37.509
Based on an anime that's based on a manga,
Mob Psycho 100 is about a quiet middle schooler

00:06:37.509 --> 00:06:40.759
who begins developing dangerous psychic powers.

00:06:40.759 --> 00:06:44.779
All he wants to do is have a normal life,
but to do that he'll have to figure out a

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:48.120
way to control his powers, and his emotions.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:51.999
The upcoming live-action series drops on May
22nd.

00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:54.729
Terrace House: Opening New Doors: Part 2

00:06:54.729 --> 00:07:00.120
This unusual Japanese reality show is something
of a sleeper hit with Western audiences, offering

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.389
a glimpse into the lives of a group of young
people living together in the same house.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:08.759
Opening New Doors is the third rendition of
the popular series and sees a new group living

00:07:08.759 --> 00:07:10.460
in a cabin in the woods.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.869
If you haven't checked it out yet, now's the
time.

00:07:12.869 --> 00:07:18.809
Part 2 of Terrace House: Opening New Doors
hits Netflix on May 22nd.

00:07:18.809 --> 00:07:19.809
Explained

00:07:19.809 --> 00:07:21.889
Ever wondered how cryptocurrencies work?

00:07:21.889 --> 00:07:24.870
How about what goes on behind the scenes of
the K-pop industry?

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:30.050
Netflix's new docuseries Explained looks into
obscure topics like these to shed light on

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.199
some of the oddest mysteries of our time.

00:07:32.199 --> 00:07:35.460
You can catch the whole show when it drops
on May 23rd.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.449
Fauda: Season 2

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:42.110
Possibly the highest rated show you've never
heard of, Fauda is an Israeli political thriller

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:47.099
that was voted one of 2017's best international
shows by The New York Times.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:51.590
Season 1 followed a military unit on the hunt
for a diabolical terrorist.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:55.740
If Season 2 follows in the same footsteps,
you can bet that it'll be packed with action,

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.789
drama, and political intrigue.

00:07:57.789 --> 00:07:59.710
Find out on May 24th.

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:00.919
Ibiza

00:08:00.919 --> 00:08:05.919
In this romantic comedy, Gillian Jacobs stars
as a woman who takes a working trip to Spain,

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:10.080
with her best friends in tow, and ends up
on a search for a famous DJ on the island

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.190
of Ibiza.

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:16.009
Phoebe Robinson and Saturday Night Live's
Vanessa Bayer costar, along with Game of Thrones'

00:08:16.009 --> 00:08:17.139
Richard Madden.

00:08:17.139 --> 00:08:19.110
Look for it on May 25th.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:21.370
The Toys That Made Us: Season 2

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:25.979
Netflix's documentary series The Toys That
Made Us takes a nostalgia-fueled look at some

00:08:25.979 --> 00:08:31.289
of the most iconic toys of the '80s and '90s,
from Star Wars figurines to He-Man action

00:08:31.289 --> 00:08:32.289
figures.

00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:37.539
But with only four episodes in the first season,
fans were definitely clamoring for more.

00:08:37.539 --> 00:08:42.310
Season 2 will delve into the rich stories
behind even more toys, with Legos guaranteed

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:47.320
on the horizon as well as a deep dive into
the numerous disasters that plagued Star Trek

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.320
toys.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.420
Look for it on May 25th.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.780
Trollhunters: Part 3

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:57.761
Few animated shows have garnered as much praise,
or been surrounded by as much tragedy, as

00:08:57.761 --> 00:08:59.780
Dreamworks' Trollhunters.

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:04.630
Spearheaded by Guillermo del Toro, the show
is about a boy who uses a magical amulet to

00:09:04.630 --> 00:09:07.020
travel to the realm of trolls.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:11.260
After the passing of Anton Yelchin, who voiced
the main character, del Toro decided to go

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:15.880
ahead and release Part 2 as Yelchin's vocals
were already recorded.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:20.310
What direction they'll take in Part 3 remains
to be seen, but we'll all find out on May

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.310
25th.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.690
Sara's Notebook

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:27.280
Years after Laura's sister goes missing in
the Congo, a photo turns up that may give

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:30.050
Laura a clue to her sister's whereabouts.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:34.710
She decides to head deep into the jungle to
track down her sister and get her home safely.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:38.330
Filled with high-stakes adventure and drama,
Sarah's Notebook looks like a sure winner

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.830
for Netflix this month.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.270
Look for it on May 26th.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.420
The Break with Michelle Wolf

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:48.520
Netflix has enjoyed some success with its
weekly series like The Joel McHale Show and

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:52.920
My Next Guest with David Letterman, and they're
apparently eager to explore the format a little

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:53.920
more.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:57.880
The Break with Michelle Wolf will see The
Daily Show's Michelle Wolf hosting a weekly

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.740
sketch comedy show.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:03.700
Netflix hasn't released many details yet,
so we'll all have to wait until May 27th to

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.680
find out what it's all about.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.160
Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt: Season 4

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.760
Three seasons after leaving her underground
cult bunker, Kimmy Schmidt is still going

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:13.760
strong.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:18.160
Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt returns for a fourth
season on May 30th.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:19.490
Original stand-up comedy

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:22.490
Big changes are on the horizon for stand-up
fans this May.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:27.320
John Mulaney kicks off the month with his
new special Kid Gorgeous Live at Radio City,

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:31.380
and on the 8th, look for Hari Kondabolu : Warn
Your Relatives.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:36.590
On May 13, Ali Wong takes shots at parenthood,
children, and pregnancy with her brand-new

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:41.700
special Hard Knock Wife, followed by Tig Notaro
Happy to Be Here on May 22.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:47.010
Finally, May 25th sees the reunion of comedy
greats Steve Martin and Martin Short as they

00:10:47.010 --> 00:10:51.210
land on Netflix with An Evening You Will Forget
for the Rest of Your Life.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.400
That's all the Netflix originals coming in
May.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:57.310
Now let's turn to all the other movies and
shows you can look forward to this month.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:58.310
New movies

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:02.960
It's high-stakes action all the way this May,
with new highlights like The Bourne Ultimatum

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:07.240
and Hellboy II: The Golden Army coming to
Netflix's lineup on the 1st of the month.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:11.500
You'll also be able to scare up plenty of
laughs, with a whole host of new comedy films

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.670
making their way to the streaming service.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:18.580
The first of the month will see Amelie, Beautiful
Girls, Harold &amp; Kumar Escape from Guantanamo

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:21.250
Bay, and The Clapper, to name a few.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:24.640
May also marks the arrival of some great new
dramas.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:28.960
On the 14th, check out The Phantom of the
Opera, and the day after that, look for Only

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.440
God Forgives.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:32.820
That's definitely a selection to get excited
about.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:37.850
For brand new documentaries, keep your eyes
peeled for 27: Gone Too Soon, a fascinating

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:43.130
glimpse into the surprisingly long list of
rockers who passed away at the age of 27.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:47.710
That arrives on the first, along with A Life
of Its Own: The Truth About Medical Marijuana

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:48.940
and The Carter Effect.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:53.530
And if the kids aren't excited about a new
pot documentary, don't worry: Family time

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:59.020
is going to get even better in May, with over
half a dozen new releases hitting Netflix.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:03.280
Highlights include Shrek on the first and
Bridge to Terabithia on the 19th.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:07.800
And on the 29th, Netflix is bringing in Disney
Pixar's Coco.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:12.260
Netflix is also sneaking some brand new chillers
and thrillers into their selection, with plenty

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:16.460
of great films to scare the pants off even
the most die-hard horror fan.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:21.820
Several classics are showing up in May, including
Red Dragon and Scream 2, both of which arrive

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:22.820
on the first.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:25.910
"I'm gonna blame the movies."

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.090
New television

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:31.480
On the television front, viewers will have
plenty to choose from this may.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:35.730
If you're looking for kids' shows, Netflix
has you covered with Season 1 of Barbie Dreamhouse

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.110
Adventures and Season 2 of Yu-Gi-Oh!

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.440
Arc-V on the first.

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:45.060
For more grown-up fare, look out for new seasons
of Girlfriends' Guide to Divorce on the 15th,

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.240
Scandal on the 19th, and Shooter on the 22nd.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.900
Thanks for watching!

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.630
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

